1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,520
A company can say, request received,

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,080
while the customer still carries every
follow-up.

3
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:08,160
DueBack keeps that promise open until

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:11,440
the evidence matches the outcome the
person actually approved.

5
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,940
Here is a synthetic refund case.

6
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,680
The store promised $59 for Order 1842,

7
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,820
but the refund has not arrived.

8
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,740
Gemini reads this source

9
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:24,040
asynchronously and proposes a typed

10
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:28,580
Outcome Contract: responsible party,
amount, reference, deadline,

11
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:34,120
citations, and uncertainty. The source
is retained for no more than 24 hours.

12
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,920
Gemini has no contact tools,

13
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:40,300
cannot approve an action, and cannot
decide that the case is done.

14
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:42,500
Now I review what it understood.

15
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,400
The contract requires signed company

16
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:48,680
evidence for this exact outcome and
reference.

17
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:51,200
{\an2}Before anything leaves DueBack, the

18
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,800
{\an2}approval boundary shows the exact
recipient,

19
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,000
{\an2}channel, proof requirement,

20
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,160
{\an2}attempt limit, and authorized path.

21
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:00,340
{\an2}This accelerated route contacts only

22
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,340
{\an2}DueBack's isolated merchant simulator.

23
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:04,920
{\an2}It cannot spend money, change the

24
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,300
{\an2}requested outcome, add new data, or

25
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:08,900
{\an2}contact an arbitrary company.

26
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,740
I authorize only this versioned plan.

27
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:15,220
From this point, the run is
continuous.

28
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:18,160
The browser is not executing the
workflow.

29
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,920
Firestore stores the approved state,

30
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:22,180
and Cloud Tasks resumes the case in

31
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:25,300
the background with authenticated,
idempotent delivery.

32
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:27,720
The first signed company reply

33
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,220
includes the right reference and

34
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:32,440
amount, but says only that the request
was received.

35
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:34,340
Acknowledgement is not proof.

36
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:38,200
The deterministic verifier rejects it,

37
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,680
so DueBack keeps the case open and

38
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,460
performs the next bounded attempt.

39
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:45,060
The controlled merchant then returns

40
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:47,200
signed evidence, confirming the exact

41
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:50,780
outcome, amount, currency, and
reference.

42
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,060
A deterministic verifier, not the

43
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:54,780
model, accepts that evidence.

44
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:57,320
The result says precisely what was

45
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:00,460
proved. The company confirmed the
refund instruction.

46
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:03,620
It also preserves the important
limitation.

47
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,840
Bank settlement is not verified, so

48
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:08,740
the person must still check the
underlying payment account.

49
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,260
{\an8}The product trace shows the same

50
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:13,660
{\an8}redacted trace suffix across approval,

51
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:16,380
{\an8}Firestore transitions, the cloud task,

52
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:18,860
{\an8}rejected acknowledgement, and accepted

53
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:21,680
{\an8}proof. It also records the real Gemini

54
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:25,500
{\an8}latency, token usage, and estimated
model cost.

55
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:28,900
{\an8}Missing telemetry would remain labeled
missing.

56
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,560
{\an8}DueBack does not manufacture evidence.

57
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:34,360
Here is the deployed back end on
Google Cloud.

58
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:37,380
Cloud Run serves the current product
revision.

59
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,560
Cloud Tasks provides bounded delivery
and retry.

60
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,980
Firestore persists the versioned case.

61
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:47,600
{\an8}The product trace records the Gemini
invocation.

62
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:52,100
The merchant simulator is a separate
Cloud Run service

63
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:56,540
with its own service account, distinct
from the DueBack runtime.

64
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:00,000
{\an2\pos(192,350)}The architecture keeps authority and
proof outside the model.

65
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,040
{\an2\pos(192,350)}Gemini and Genkit propose typed facts.

66
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,560
{\an2\pos(192,350)}The person approves an exact boundary.

67
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:09,700
{\an2\pos(192,350)}Firestore and Cloud Tasks persist and
resume the work.

68
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:12,900
{\an2\pos(192,350)}The action broker releases only
approved fields.

69
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:16,960
{\an2\pos(192,350)}Signed evidence returns through a
deterministic verifier, and only

70
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:19,900
{\an2\pos(192,350)}sufficient evidence can close the
case.

71
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,700
DueBack is a Taskmaster entry built
by one individual

72
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:25,140
for the All Things Agentic Hackathon.

73
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,000
Delegate the chase.

74
00:03:27,020 --> 00:03:28,220
Keep the proof.
